"J-join-mira": "mira makes light of things that still frighten me. she starts teasing, then seems to forget where she was going with it.\nit doesn't feel like she's trying to hurt me. i still worry she'll miss something dangerous.\ni hope i can keep up with her and keep us both safe.",
"J-join-sorrel": "sorrel gives me facts when i'm hoping for something comforting.\nshe doesn't make them sound any kinder than they are. i'm not sure what to say to her yet.\ni want to understand enough that i don't put her in danger by guessing.",
"J-join-brunn": {
"A": "brunn seems to carry everyone outside these halls into camp with him. stopping this matters to him more than getting any rest.\nhis sarcasm hurts. when he picks at mira, he means it, and she pushes back.\nthere are four of us now, but it feels heavier, not easier. i worry about what all of us are taking farther in.",
"B": "brunn's grief for the people he lost is here at camp too. i don't know what i could say that would help.\nit hasn't made his words gentle. he picks at mira as if he wants to hurt her, and she won't just take it.\nthere are four of us now. i feel the weight of keeping us alive more than before."
},
"J-awhile-mira": "i'm getting used to mira starting one thought and wandering into another.\nshe still finds things to tease me about when i'm worrying. sometimes i have to ask what she meant.\ni'm learning when she's only playing. i still have trouble leaving my worries alone.",
"J-awhile-sorrel": "i'm getting used to the quiet after sorrel answers me. usually she's already said everything she thinks i need to know.\ni keep wanting to ask if she's sure. she gives me the facts again, no warmer the second time.\ni'm trying to listen properly the first time.",
"J-awhile-brunn": "i can hear the bite coming in brunn's voice now. it isn't a joke just because he says it with sarcasm.\nhe keeps picking at mira, and she keeps defending herself. i worry about how much of that she has to put up with.\nbeing used to it doesn't make it easy to sit beside.",
"J-grow-mira": "i've started looking forward to mira's teasing. even when she loses her own point halfway through, i'm glad she's here.\nit doesn't make the danger smaller. sometimes it gives me a moment when danger isn't the only thing i can think about.\ni care about her. i want her to get out of here still herself.",
"J-grow-sorrel": "i'm glad sorrel doesn't tell me something comforting just because i want it.\nshe's still cold about it. but i've come to value knowing which things we can count on, and which we can't.\ni'd like her to get the answers she wants. i want her alive to have them.",
"J-grow-brunn": "i've come to care whether brunn makes it through this, not just whether he can help us through a fight.\nhe still wants someone to pay. his sarcasm still cuts, and caring about him doesn't make what he says to mira right.\ni want him to have a life beyond the next thing he can hit. i don't know if he wants that yet.",
"J-party-family": "these three feel more like a family to me than dad ever did. i'm worried about writing that down.\nmira still wanders off into her own thoughts. sorrel is cold, and brunn can be cruel. being together hasn't made us easy people to sit with.\nbut i feel part of us. i still worry about dad at home. both things are true.",
"J-shame-dad": "i'm ashamed of my dad. recognizing him in that picture hasn't left me alone tonight.\nit feels wrong to know this much about him and still not know what to do with it.\ni can barely put his name beside what we've walked through. i wish i didn't keep wanting to look away.",
"J-picnic-reveal": "i've never seen dad look that happy. i keep remembering his face in the picnic picture.\nmom was beautiful. i wish i'd had the chance to meet her.\ni wish i could have sat with them for a little while. just an ordinary afternoon, with nothing i had to fix.",
"J-bedside-hate": "i hate my dad tonight. i can name him now, and i can't keep what he did apart from the ruin we've been walking through.\ni have nothing but contempt for those actions. other people have had to suffer through what he left.\ni came here wanting him well. i still don't want anyone else hurt. i don't know how to carry all of that together.",
"J-zone5-mystery": "who is the person in these pictures? i keep thinking about him now that we're at camp.\nmaybe he's the cause of this. maybe he's too ashamed to let his face be seen.\ni don't know. i'm frightened of guessing wrong, but i can't stop wondering.",
"J-zone5-stitch": "i'm trying to fit the new pictures from these halls beside the bedside one. i know it's dad now.\neach new piece makes me look back at what i thought i understood. i can put more of it together, but there are still gaps.\ni want to keep straight what i actually saw and what i'm only afraid might fit."
